    <DataNode elementId="AT3G56940-MONOMER" textLabel="AT3G56940-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9M591" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="415" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">&lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; mutants (&lt;i&gt;chl27-as&lt;/i&gt;)affected in the &lt;i&gt;AtCHL27&lt;/i&gt; gene accumulate magnesium-protoporphyrin IX monomethyl ester (MgPMME) whilst the major compounds in extracts of wildtype plants was identified as protochlorophyllide (Pchlide), demonstrating that those mutant plants are blocked at the cyclase step |CITS:[14673103]|. The aerobic cyclase reaction involves three proposed steps including i) the stereospecific hydroxylation of the methyl-esterified ring C propionate followed by ii) the oxidation of the alcohol to the corresponding ketone; the activated methylene group reacts with the &amp;gamma;-meso carbon of the porphyrin nucleus in an oxidative reaction involving the removal of two H to yield ring E |CITS:[3202840]|. Although the study of the &lt;i&gt;chl27-as&lt;/i&gt; mutants could not dismiss the involvement of &lt;i&gt;AtCHL27&lt;/i&gt; in regulatory rather than chemical functions, the predicted iron-containing active site and conserved cysteines of &lt;i&gt;AtCHL27&lt;/i&gt; suggests an involvement in the latter |CITS:[14673103]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G56940-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G56940.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9M591" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pid" value="NP_191253" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33389, RXN-12165, RXN-12164, RXN-12163" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="4" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0042651" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT3G56940.1" />
