    <DataNode elementId="AT4G25080-MONOMER" textLabel="magnesium protoporphyrin IX methyltransferase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SW18" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; gene &lt;i&gt;CHLM&lt;/i&gt; was heterologously expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt; and was shown to encode for a protein with magnesium protoporphyrin IX methyltransferase activity which catalyzes the conversion of Mg-protoporphyrin IX into methyl-Mg-protoporphyrin IX |CITS:[11784318]|. This nuclear-encoded protein is translocated to the chloroplast. It is synthesized with an N-terminal chloroplastic targeting sequence which needs to be processed for the protein to be fully active |CITS:[11784318]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G25080-MONOMER" />
