      <Comment>Mg-chelatase-catalyzed insertion of magnesium into protoporphyrin IX. Mg-chelatase is composed of both soluble and membrane-bound protein(s) |CITS: [11607197]|. In higher plants three proteins are necessary for the Mg chelation. In &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;, the complex is thought to be formed of the three subunits: D, H and I (the corresponding proteins are called CHLD, CHLH and CHLI) |CITS:[11172074]|. Mutants with lesions in the I (&lt;i&gt;cs&lt;/i&gt; mutant) and D (&lt;i&gt;cch&lt;/i&gt; mutant) subunits have been shown to produce 74% and 28% of the magnesium protoporphyrin IX monoethyl ester, and the &lt;i&gt;cch&lt;/i&gt; mutant was also shown to accumulate more protoporphyrin IX than wildtype |CITS:[11172074]|. The enzymatic activities of the proteins constitutive of the magnesium chelatase complex in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; largely remain to be confirmed by direct assays.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="CPLX1F-78" />
